# `linodenet.parametrize` Module

This module is an alternative to `torch.nn.utils.parametrizations` that provides JIT-compatible parametrizations for PyTorch models.
The central difference is the internal mechanism for applying parametrizations, which is designed to be compatible with TorchScript (JIT).

- the builtin mechanism substitutes the parametrized tensor with a `@property` that holds the parametrization logic.
  - in particular, it is evaluated at every access, which is very slow without caching if the parametrization is complex and the tensor is accessed frequently
  - this is especially problematic in sequential (RNN/GRU/LSTM) models.
- Our method replaces the tensor with a `buffer` that holds the cached parametrization.
  - we always use the parametrized value immediately
  - we need to manually update the buffer when the base tensor changes (e.g. after an optimizer step)
